  "conclusions": [
    "HTTP and TLS legacy true+IPIfNonMatch controls still emit the wrong original IPv4; replacing only routeOnly still selects direct under a synthetic China DNS answer. These are expected negative controls, not assertions that legacy policy is correct.",
    "For both HTTP and TLS, false+AsIs emits the sniffed domain in the actual VLESS destination header under synthetic China and private DNS answers.",
    "The bigmodel/geosite-China and literal China/private-IP direct controls retain their expected routing behavior on the new core."
  ],
  "limits": [
    "Only loopback exists in the new network namespace. The original destination is fixed in the fixture instead of production nft/SO_ORIGINAL_DST; this is not a host transparent-routing or cgroup integration acceptance.",
    "The VLESS receiver, DNS mappings and freedom sink are controlled local substitutes. TLS uses a ClientHello/SNI only, without an upstream TLS handshake, signed-in account or inference.",
    "No current service selection, host nft rules, credentials, real external MCP, public DNS or commercial provider was touched by these12 tests. Service preservation applies to this test window; subsequent root-authorized deployment is separate.",
    "This routing regression does not independently verify every security fix in the new upstream release, including MPTCP behavior. Official download/metadata verification belongs to the separate prepare evidence.",
    "No full suite was rerun. Original26.10.29 scripts/result/report remain byte-identical and new26.10.31 evidence is separate."
  ],
